GalleonCore for Ubuntu 24.04 and later (Qt >= 6.4)

Install with: sudo apt install ./galleoncore_0.2.1-1_amd64.deb
Enable from your graphical session, without sudo:
  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user enable --now galleond.service
Start settings from the application menu or run galleon-bosun.
Before removing the package:
  systemctl --user disable --now galleond.service

The package never enables or starts the user service automatically.
udev grants access to the active local session. Reconnect the device if needed.
uinput is loaded on installation (best effort) and at the next boot.
FFmpeg is recommended for video features. Screensaver videos and the OpenRGB
plugin are not included. User configuration is preserved on removal/purge.
